# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# On 'unsafe-inline', which we would rather not need:
#
#   style-src  — Radix positions its overlays and Motion animates by writing inline
#                style attributes. Both are locked stack choices, so inline styles are
#                a requirement, not an oversight.
#   script-src — Astro emits a small inline bootstrap on every page that hydrates an
#                island. Its experimental CSP flag can hash those scripts, but it also
#                forces hashes onto style-src, and a hash in the source list makes the
#                browser ignore 'unsafe-inline' — which silently kills every Radix and
#                Motion animation. Hash-strict scripts and working islands are not
#                currently available at the same time.
#
# The fix, when it exists, is per-directive control in Astro's CSP support, or a Pages
# Function issuing a per-response nonce. Until then the XSS defence is the layer that
# actually matters here: React escapes everything, nothing uses dangerouslySetInnerHTML,
# and file input is validated before it is touched.
#
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' is not the same permission as 'unsafe-eval', despite the name: it
# only allows compiling a WebAssembly module, not evaluating a JS string, and Chrome
# refuses WebAssembly.instantiate() without it — confirmed by actually enforcing this
# policy in a browser, not assumed. The Image Converter's codecs (@jsquash/*, heic-to)
# are the first thing in the suite that touches WebAssembly at all; nothing before it
# needed the keyword, which is why it wasn't here already.
#
# connect-src carries two Hugging Face hosts for the Background Remover: huggingface.co
# itself, where the model file's metadata and redirect are served from, and *.hf.co,
# the CDN the redirect actually resolves to (traced with a real request rather than
# assumed — the exact subdomain is signed and rotates, so the wildcard is the only
# stable target). The model file is the one thing in the suite that isn't self-hosted:
# it's a public, cacheable download that never carries anything about the visitor or
# their photo, which stays on-device like every other tool. The WASM engine that runs
# it is still self-hosted (public/ort/, copied from onnxruntime-web at install time)
# rather than pulled from jsDelivr, so this is the only third-party host the CSP trusts.
#
# Everything else stays locked down. blob: is allowed for images, media and workers
# because tools preview and download their own output through object URLs — never a
# remote fetch.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; frame-src 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://huggingface.co https://*.hf.co; worker-src 'self' blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# ffmpeg.wasm needs SharedArrayBuffer, which needs full cross-origin isolation. Scope
# COEP to the video route when that tool lands rather than turning it on site-wide,
# where it would block anything the other tools legitimately load.

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
